  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  margin: 0 0 1rem;
}
lion-input, lion-button {
  display: block;
  max-width: 24rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}
`;

      // The three demos, named the way a developer splits an app — by where the code runs — with the shim-layer term
      // each one used to carry kept as the quieter subtitle. Every file lives under `client/` or `server/`.
      // Paths in the server code are relative: the working directory is the project root, under real Node as here,
