`,
            'client/styles.css': canvasStyles,
          },
        },
        server: {
          label: 'server',
          hint: 'node',
          note: 'server/ is what a server runs: main.js reads server/data.json, writes out.txt, prints to stdout and starts a worker thread that answers with a message. There is no real server — this runs in your browser, against an in-memory filesystem and a dependency-free layer that answers Node’s API (fs, path, process, os, util, events, url, worker_threads); the worker is a real Web Worker. A server has no page, so its result is the console.',
